  "body": "Stacked on #2192 (base `issue/2181-sim-precalc`). Retarget this PR to `main` before #2192 merges.\r\n\r\n## What changed\r\n\r\n- The stock playback (the transport's traced stock) plays the program in posting order up to the first operation that has no toolpath. It stops there. It does not skip that operation to cut the operations after it.\r\n  - `posting::program_ops_until_ungenerated` and `stock_sim::plan_program_until_ungenerated` are new. Only `PlaySeed::gather` uses them.\r\n  - `posting::program_ops` and `stock_sim::plan_program` keep their behaviour. The post and the Deviate verdict still refuse the program by name (\"<op>: no toolpath yet - generate it first\").\r\n  - `PlayIndex::stop()` names the operation. `PlayIndex::position_at` holds the stock at the end of the plan when the playhead is on an operation at or after the stop.\r\n  - When the first operation has no toolpath, the playback shows the uncut stock of that operation's setup.\r\n- A separate line under the transport bar names the stop: \"Stock simulation stops before 2D Contour1: it has no toolpath. Generate it to see the rest.\" (`play_precalc::stop_readout`, `play_precalc::transport_row`). The stop is not added to the status line. Thus the generation notes of a clean operation do not get the \"!\" error mark.\r\n- The remaining playback refusal reads \"simulation shows the uncut stock: <why>\". It replaces \"traced playback refused: <why> - the sheet stands\".\r\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/2280-sim-partial-playback.md`.\r\n\r\n## Safety\r\n\r\nThe stock judgment that can block the post does not change. `simulate_document`, `verification_gate` and the post walk `program_ops` as before. The pinning test asserts that `simulate_document` and `program_ops` still refuse the same document.\r\n\r\n## Pinning tests\r\n\r\n- `crates/app/tests/stock_play_stop.rs`\r\n  - `playback_plays_the_ops_before_the_first_one_without_a_toolpath`: the end of the playback equals the stock of the document with Face1 only; the verdict and the post still refuse.\r\n  - `playback_never_skips_an_op_without_a_toolpath_to_cut_the_next`: the first operation has no toolpath; the generated second operation is not cut.\r\n  - `a_whole_program_has_no_stop`.\r\n- `crates/ui/src/play_precalc_tests.rs::an_op_without_a_toolpath_stops_the_playback_and_says_so`: the playback runs, the stop text is pinned, the status line is not changed.\r\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/status_alert.rs::the_notes_of_a_clean_operation_are_not_an_alert`: the notes from the issue do not carry the error mark.\r\n- Updated: `field_view_tests::a_refused_playback_is_said_once_and_retired_with_the_transport` (new refusal words).\r\n\r\n## Readings\r\n\r\n- app (`cargo test -p camcraft-app`): `stock_play_stop` 3 passed; `stock_play` 7 passed; `stock_play_precalc` 7 passed (1 ignored, heavy lane); `stock_sim_document` 9 passed.\r\n- ui (`cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib`, CWD `crates/ui`): `play_precalc` 3 passed; `status_alert` 5 passed; `field_view_tests` 3 passed.\r\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\r\n- All on head ba987e7b4.\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n\r\n- The GUI was not started. The line under the transport bar was not seen on screen.\r\n- The quick tier was not run; only the targeted tests above and clippy for `camcraft-app` and `camcraft-ui`.\r\n- `crates/ui/src/machined.rs` and `crates/ui/src/egui_app/view_pass.rs` still say \"the sheet stands\" in two other refusals. They are not in the playback path of this issue.\r\n\r\nChangelog: The stock simulation now plays up to the first operation that has no toolpath, and a separate line names that operation, instead of refusing the whole setup.\r\n\r\nEffort: high\r\n\r\nFixes #2280\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
